WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.610 align:center size:90%
To begin today’s video
blog, I wanted to recall

2
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.590 align:center size:90%
a text I found on day 3, which talks about

3
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.600 align:center size:90%
rhythm. To dance, dance

4
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.100 align:center size:90%
gently, with small movements,
without taking up space,

5
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.910 align:center size:90%
if you know what I mean.

6
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.120 align:center size:90%
It comes before the beat, because some

7
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.580 align:center size:90%
people confuse rhythm with metre,

8
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.430 align:center size:90%
but they’re not the same.

9
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.310 align:center size:90%
Look,

10
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.500 align:center size:90%
I know plenty of people

11
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.630 align:center size:90%
with a great sense of metre,

12
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.374 align:center size:90%
but it’s not the same.

13
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.000 align:center size:90%
I’ve been told that rhythm
comes from who you are.

14
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:50.970 align:center size:90%
As you are,

15
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.719 align:center size:90%
so is your rhythm.
